---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const skills = ['Azure', 'AWS', 'Kubernetes', 'Terraform', 'CI/CD', 'GitHub Actions', 'Platform engineering', 'Cloud security', 'Automation', 'AI-augmented engineering'];
const aiPractices = [
	{ title: 'AI pair-programming for infrastructure', body: 'Using AI coding agents to draft Terraform, Helm and pipeline changes, then reviewing and testing them like any other code.' },
	{ title: 'AI-assisted code and security review', body: 'Adding AI reviewers to pull requests and security scans so issues surface earlier and humans spend their time on the calls that matter.' },
	{ title: 'Faster incident insight', body: 'Letting AI summarise alerts, logs and traces into a clear starting point, which shortens the path from "something is wrong" to "here is the fix".' },
	{ title: 'Governed AI tooling', body: 'Connecting AI agents to cloud platforms through controlled tool access (such as MCP servers), with least privilege, auditability and a human approving every change.' },
];
---

<Base title="Isaac Egglestone | DevOps & Platform Engineer">
	<h1>Hi, I'm Isaac.</h1>
	<p>
		I'm a DevOps and platform engineer based in Melbourne. I build and run cloud platforms on Azure, AWS and
		Kubernetes, manage infrastructure as code with Terraform, and automate delivery pipelines so engineering teams
		can ship safely and quickly.
	</p>
	<p>
		Increasingly, I'm using AI to make all of that better: faster feedback, safer changes and less toil, with
		people staying firmly in control.
	</p>
	<ul class="tags">
		{skills.map((skill) => <li>{skill}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<figure>
		<img src="/images/devops-ai-infinity.svg" alt="DevOps infinity loop (plan, code, build, test, release, deploy, operate, monitor) with AI at the centre assisting every stage" width="900" height="440" />
	</figure>

	<h2>Leveraging AI across DevOps</h2>
	<p>
		DevOps is all about feedback loops. AI makes each loop tighter by helping at every stage, from writing the
		change to understanding how it behaves in production.
	</p>
	<div class="cards">
		{aiPractices.map((p) => (
			<section class="card">
				<h3>{p.title}</h3>
				<p>{p.body}</p>
			</section>
		))}
	</div>

	<figure>
		<img src="/images/ai-pipeline.svg" alt="Delivery pipeline: commit, AI code review, build, AI security scan triage, deploy with Terraform and Helm, observe with AI incident insights, and a feedback path back to commit" width="900" height="320" loading="lazy" />
	</figure>

	<figure>
		<img src="/images/ai-feedback-loop.svg" alt="Operations feedback loop: observe, AI analysis, AI-suggested fixes, human review, act through infrastructure as code, and learn" width="900" height="600" loading="lazy" />
	</figure>

	<h2>Projects</h2>
	<p class="muted">Portfolio projects are on the way. In the meantime, see my work on <a href="https://github.com/isaacegglestone">GitHub</a>.</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>Connect with me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/isaacegglestone/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
</Base>
